language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Find a series of the pitch classes 0 to n-1, each used once, whose neighbouring intervals are exactly the values 1 to n-1, each once.
given n : int
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..n-1)
find diffs : matrix indexed by [int(1..n-1)] of int(1..n-1)

branching on [diffs, x]

such that
$ the series is a permutation of the pitch classes 0 to n-1
allDiff(x),
$ each interval is the absolute difference of two neighbouring pitch classes
forAll i : int(1..n-1) . diffs[i] = |x[i+1] - x[i]|,
$ the intervals between neighbouring notes are all different, so they cover the full set 1 to n-1
allDiff(diffs)
